summary:
Here is the complete picture of how owner creation (`POST /owners`) works in this OfficeFloor-based PetClinic.

## Build file and running tests

- Build file: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (Maven; Spring Boot parent). Maven wrapper present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`.
- Run the full suite: `./mvnw test` (unit/surefire) or `./mvnw verify`. There is no `target/` yet, so the first build also generates sources.
- DTOs are NOT hand-written source files. They are generated by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`, package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, with a `Dto` name suffix (so `OwnerFields` schema -> `OwnerFieldsDto`, `Owner` -> `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPage` -> `OwnerPageDto`). This is why no `OwnerFieldsDto.java`/`OwnerDto.java` exists under `src/`.

## 1. Owner endpoint YAMLs (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`)

The directory also contains `owners.GET.yml`, `v2/owners.GET.yml`, and `owners/{ownerId}.{GET,PUT,DELETE}.yml`. The creation one is `owners.POST.yml`:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: normalize

normalize:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: ensureUniqueTelephone

ensureUniqueTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignCustomerCode

assignCustomerCode:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignCustomerCode
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

So the POST chain is: **ValidateOwner → NormalizeOwnerTelephone → EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone → BuildOwner → AssignCustomerCode → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated**, all under role `OWNER_ADMIN` and a `transaction` governance.

Related endpoint YAMLs for context:
- `owners.GET.yml` → `ListOwners` (readonly-transaction)
- `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` → `LoadOwner` → `RespondWithOwner`
- `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` → `ValidateOwner` → `LoadOwner` → `ApplyOwner` → `SaveOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`
- `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml` → `LoadOwner` → `DeleteOwner` → `common.RespondWithNoContent`

## 2. Java function classes in the POST chain

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

`ValidateOwner.java`
