- DTOs are NOT hand-written source files. They are generated by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`, package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, with a `Dto` name suffix (so `OwnerFields` schema -> `OwnerFieldsDto`, `Owner` -> `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPage` -> `OwnerPageDto`). This is why no `OwnerFieldsDto.java`/`OwnerDto.java` exists under `src/`.

## 1. Owner endpoint YAMLs (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`)

The directory also contains `owners.GET.yml`, `v2/owners.GET.yml`, and `owners/{ownerId}.{GET,PUT,DELETE}.yml`. The creation one is `owners.POST.yml`:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: normalize

normalize:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: ensureUniqueTelephone

ensureUniqueTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignCustomerCode

assignCustomerCode:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignCustomerCode
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

So the POST chain is: **ValidateOwner → NormalizeOwnerTelephone → EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone → BuildOwner → AssignCustomerCode → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated**, all under role `OWNER_ADMIN` and a `transaction` governance.

Related endpoint YAMLs for context:
- `owners.GET.yml` → `ListOwners` (readonly-transaction)
- `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` → `LoadOwner` → `RespondWithOwner`
- `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` → `ValidateOwner` → `LoadOwner` → `ApplyOwner` → `SaveOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`
- `owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml` → `LoadOwner` → `DeleteOwner` → `common.RespondWithNoContent`

## 2. Java function classes in the POST chain

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

`ValidateOwner.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import jakarta.validation.Valid;
import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.validation.annotation.Validated;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;

/**
 * Validates before {@link LoadOwner} runs, so an invalid body is a 400 even when the owner does not exist.
 */
@Validated
public class ValidateOwner {

    public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated) {
        validated.set(request);
    }
}
```

`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneException;

/**
 * Normalizes the submitted telephone on create into E.164 form via {@link OwnerTelephones}.
 * ...
 */
public class NormalizeOwnerTelephone {

    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
        String telephone = request.getTelephone();
        String e164 = OwnerTelephones.toE164(telephone);
        if (e164 == null) {
            throw new InvalidTelephoneException(telephone);
        }
        request.setTelephone(e164);
    }
}
```

`EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.OwnerRepository;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException;

/**
 * Rejects creating an owner whose E.164 telephone is already used by any other owner.
 * ...
 */
public class EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone {

    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
        String telephone = request.getTelephone();
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (telephone.equals(OwnerTelephones.toE164(existing.getTelephone()))) {
                throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

`BuildOwner.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.time.LocalDate;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;

public class BuildOwner {

    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
        owner.setEmail(OwnerEmails.normalize(request.getEmail()));
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
        }
        built.set(owner);
    }
}
```

`AssignCustomerCode.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.util.Locale;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.OwnerRepository;

/**
 * Assigns the owner's {@code customerCode}, formatted {@code <LAST3>-<NNNN>} ...
 */
public class AssignCustomerCode {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String lastName = owner.getLastName();
        String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
        int sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1;
        owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%04d", last3, sequence));
    }
}
```

